# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
# Per-machine VS Code settings. The repo is worked from the MacBook Pro, the
# iMac, and the OptiPlex, and the paths and toolchains differ on each.
.vscode/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings (permissions, model, etc). .claude/skills/
# is tracked on purpose — only local settings.json is excluded.
.claude/settings.json

# Python bytecode (io-dashboard/tools)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OneDrive placeholder / cache files
*.cloud
*.cloudf
desktop.ini

# NotebookLM / other HTML cache folders
*_cache/
*.nblm/

# Raw photo/video media — keep these in cloud storage, not in git.
# (photos/README.md is tracked; media files are ignored.)
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.heic
*.heif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv

# Obsidian editor state.
# This repo is no longer maintained as an Obsidian vault (2026-08-23). Nothing
# under .obsidian/ is tracked; if you open the repo in Obsidian anyway, its
# config stays local to your machine. Plugin settings can hold API keys and this
# repo is public, so this must stay ignored.
.obsidian/

# LinuxCNC / Mesa runtime outputs kept locally, not committed
mesa_readhmid.txt
mesa_hal_pins.txt
linuxcnc.var.bak
*.var.bak

# Shareable single-file build of the I/O Navigator (tools/build_standalone.py).
# Derived from index.html + the CSS/JS in this folder — rebuild it, never commit it.
io-dashboard/dist/

# Camera-roll grouping output (scripts/photo_tools/group_photos.py).
# These are generated per-run and must never be committed: groups.json and
# apply_plan.sh list the absolute path, filename and exact capture time of
# every photo in the library, and this repo is PUBLIC (CLAUDE.md, owner
# decision 2026-08-22). That is a personal-activity timeline, not a build
# artefact. An auto-sync commit published three runs' worth on 2026-08-25
# before this rule existed.
# Regenerate instead: python3 scripts/photo_tools/group_photos.py --photos-library
photo-grouping-report/
photo-grouping-report-*/
